ary-json, repo-exposure-md, repo-sarif, agent-seam-packets-json.\n- `ripr diff` (full-repo context command) and `check --diff PATH` (read a diff from a file) share a name for different operations; both exist with distinct help.\n- A newcomer also faces pilot vs check, the first-pr/start-here alias, and the start-here.md artifact.\n\n#1613 delivered progressive help disclosure (one-screen top help, per-command help, `--all` with guards). The underlying choice space is unchanged: verified hands-on, the dev top help is task-oriented but every choice above still confronts a first-hour user.\n\n## Required outcome (owner decision among)\n\n- A: curate — split formats into command families (check keeps findings formats; repo/badge/packet formats move to dedicated commands), and rename or alias the overlapping diff surface;\n- B: document — keep the space, add a chooser (format groups in `--help` with one recommended path per task, and/or `help workflow`);\n- C: subset plus escape hatch — `check --format` accepts a curated few; the full list lives behind per-area commands or an explicit flag.\n\nAny direction ships migration notes for existing consumers (generated CI workflow, documented JSON/SARIF contracts, badge endpoints, agent packets).\n\n## Focused proof\n\n- [ ] The chosen direction is implemented; a newcomer walk (check, explain, pilot, first-pr on a scratch repo) names each choice unambiguously.\n- [ ] Existing consumers keep working or get a mapped path: generated CI workflow, JSON/SARIF contracts, badge endpoints.\n- [ ] Typo suggestion (`Did you mean`) and unknown-format errors cover the new surface.\n- [ ] Removal experiment: restore the 22-value single flag and prove the overload returns.\n\n## Claim boundary\n\nSurface choice only. No analysis, findings, or output-content changes. The duplicated accepted-list string is a separate mechanical cleanup issue.\n\n## Relationships\n\n- Related: #1613 (help disclosure delivered; catalog/consistency remaining — not the same claim).\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No format removals without a mapped path.\n- No new output content.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/issues/5211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/issues/5211/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]